    "q-275032": {
      "dom_id": "step-q275032",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Given that\n\n$$\nX⊙Y=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ -3 & 4\\end{aligned}]\\,Z=[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 2 \\\\ 4 & -3\\end{aligned}]\\,\\text{and}\\,\\alpha =3\n$$\n\nfind $(\\alpha Y)⊙X+{Z}^{T}.$",
      "worked_solution": "For compatible matrices $A,$ $B,$ and $C,$ and scalar $\\alpha ,$ the Hadamard product has the following properties:\n\n- Commutativity:\n\n$$\nA⊙B=B⊙A\n$$\n\n- Associativity:\n\n$$\n(A⊙B)⊙C=A⊙(B⊙C)\n$$\n\n- Distributivity over Addition:\n\n$$\nA⊙(B+C)=A⊙B+A⊙C\n$$\n\n- Scalar Distributivity:\n\n$$\n\\alpha (A⊙B)=(\\alpha A)⊙B=A⊙(\\alpha B)\n$$\n\nIn this case, by the scalar distributivity of the Hadamard product, we have\n\n$$\n(\\alpha Y)⊙X+{Z}^{T}=\\alpha (Y⊙X)+{Z}^{T}.\n$$\n\nThen, by the commutativity of the Hadamard product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\alpha (Y⊙X)+{Z}^{T} & =\\alpha (X⊙Y)+{Z}^{T} \\\\  & =3[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ -3 & 4\\end{aligned}]+{[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 2 \\\\ 4 & -3\\end{aligned}]}^{T} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}6 & -3 \\\\ -9 & 12\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 4 \\\\ 2 & -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}6-5 & -3+4 \\\\ -9+2 & 12-3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ -7 & 9\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-275032-a",
