    "q-350397": {
      "dom_id": "step-q350397",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 3 \\\\ -1 & -3\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -2\\end{aligned}],\\,y=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nGiven the matrices above, write $A{x}^{T}⊙(y+{x}^{T})$ as a matrix product.\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td rowspan=\"2\" height=\"30px\" align=\"center\">$A{x}^{T}⊙(y+{x}^{T})=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td width=\"5px\" height=\"30px\" align=\"center\"></td>\n<td width=\"30px\" align=\"center\">\n\n{{field-1}}\n\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\">\n\n$0$\n\n</td>\n<td width=\"5px\" align=\"center\"></td>\n<td width=\"7px\" height=\"30px\"></td>\n<td width=\"5px\" height=\"30px\" align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">\n\n$-5$\n\n</td>\n<td width=\"5px\" align=\"center\"></td>\n<td width=\"5px\" height=\"30px\" align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n\n<tr> \n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td width=\"30px\" align=\"center\">\n\n$0$\n\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\">\n\n{{field-2}}\n\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td width=\"5px\" height=\"30px\" align=\"center\"></td>\n<td width=\"5px\" height=\"30px\" align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">\n\n{{field-3}}\n\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td width=\"5px\" height=\"30px\" align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>",
      "worked_solution": "The Hadamard product of two compatible vectors $u$ and $v$ can be expressed as the matrix product\n\n$$\nv⊙u=\\text{diag}(v)u.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\nA{x}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 3 \\\\ -1 & -3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\ny+{x}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNotice that they are of the same size; hence, their Hadamard product is well-defined. We conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A{x}^{T}⊙(y+{x}^{T}) & =\\text{diag}(A{x}^{T})(y+{x}^{T}) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 8\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "field-1",
          "type": "blank",
