    "q-350404": {
      "dom_id": "step-q350404",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "Given that\n\n$$\nA⊙B=[\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\,\\text{and}\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}4 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nfind ${C}^{T}+B⊙A.$",
      "worked_solution": "For compatible matrices $A,$ $B,$ and $C,$ and scalar $\\alpha ,$ the Hadamard product has the following properties:\n\n- Commutativity:\n\n$$\nA⊙B=B⊙A\n$$\n\n- Associativity:\n\n$$\n(A⊙B)⊙C=A⊙(B⊙C)\n$$\n\n- Distributivity over Addition:\n\n$$\nA⊙(B+C)=A⊙B+A⊙C\n$$\n\n- Scalar Distributivity:\n\n$$\n\\alpha (A⊙B)=(\\alpha A)⊙B=A⊙(\\alpha B)\n$$\n\nIn this case, by the commutativity of the Hadamard product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{C}^{T}+B⊙A & ={C}^{T}+A⊙B \\\\  & ={[\\begin{aligned}4 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]}^{T}+[\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}9 & -2 \\\\ -4 & 3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
